{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-12-Dec-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 19, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "60%", "added": false}, {"text": "65%", "added": false}, {"text": "100%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "50%"}, {"n": 2, "text": "A rectangular aquarium with dimensions 60 cm × 45 cm × 40 cm is filled with water to 80% of its height. If a solid metallic cube of edge 20 cm is completely immersed in it, by how much does the water level rise (rounded off to two decimal places)?", "options": [{"text": "2.56 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "2.76 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "2.36 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "2.96 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "2.96 cm"}, {"n": 3, "text": "What is the third proportional to 54x2 and 18xy?4963", "options": [{"text": "4y2", "added": false}, {"text": "6y2", "added": false}, {"text": "5y2", "added": false}, {"text": "7y2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "6y2"}, {"n": 4, "text": "6514", "options": [{"text": "4.75", "added": false}, {"text": "6.25", "added": false}, {"text": "5.75", "added": false}, {"text": "5.25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "96%"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The difference between two numbers is 92. The ratio of the two numbers is 7 : 3. Which is the smaller of the two numbers?", "options": [{"text": "79", "added": false}, {"text": "96", "added": false}, {"text": "69", "added": false}, {"text": "63", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "69"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A sum of money was invested at simple interest at a certain rate for 9 years. Had it been invested at an 8% per annum higher rate, it would have fetched ₹7,992 more. Find the principal.", "options": [{"text": "₹11,100", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹11,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹12,200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "₹11,100"}, {"n": 7, "text": "If A : B = 4 : 6 and B : C = 7 : 11, then A : B : C is:", "options": [{"text": "14 : 21 : 33", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 12 : 33", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 31 : 21", "added": false}, {"text": "11 : 23 : 40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "14 : 21 : 33"}, {"n": 8, "text": "A helicopter is flying at a height of 575 m. A person on the ground sees it at an angle of elevation of 30°. What is the horizontal distance from the person to the point on the ground exactly below the helicopter?", "options": [{"text": "990.75 m", "added": false}, {"text": "896.75 m", "added": false}, {"text": "994.75 m", "added": false}, {"text": "895.75 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "heights-and-distances", "key_answer": "994.75 m"}, {"n": 9, "text": "A and B working together can do a piece of work in 6 days. B alone can do the same work in 14 days. How long (in days) will A alone take to do double the work?", "options": [{"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "10.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "21"}, {"n": 10, "text": "A 290-metre-long train crosses a platform thrice its length in 29 seconds. What is the speed of the train (in km/hr)?3716", "options": [{"text": "144", "added": false}, {"text": "147", "added": false}, {"text": "138", "added": false}, {"text": "153", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": "144"}, {"n": 11, "text": "In 10 years from now, A will be twice as old as B was 10 years ago. If A is 9 years older than B, find the present age of A.", "options": [{"text": "38 years", "added": false}, {"text": "48 years", "added": false}, {"text": "44 years", "added": false}, {"text": "40 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "48 years"}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "22530", "added": false}, {"text": "21500", "added": false}, {"text": "20110", "added": false}, {"text": "21025", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "24 cm"}, {"n": 13, "text": "Find the area of the triangle if the lengths of its two perpendicular sides are 4 cm and 5 cm.", "options": [{"text": "25 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "30 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "20 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "10 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": "10 cm2"}, {"n": 14, "text": "Find the H.C.F. of 18, 54, and 72 is:", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "18"}, {"n": 15, "text": "A class of 93 students took a Physics test. 10 students had an average score of 90. The remaining students had an average score of 75. What is the average score (rounded off to one decimal place) of the whole class?", "options": [{"text": "71.8", "added": false}, {"text": "76.6", "added": false}, {"text": "86.7", "added": false}, {"text": "74.9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "weighted-average", "key_answer": "76.6"}, {"n": 16, "text": "The arithmetic mean of the observations 27, 36, 12, 24, 48, 59, 60, 80 and 14 is:", "options": [{"text": "31", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "40"}, {"n": 17, "text": "A dealer makes a profit of 52% even after giving a 24% discount on the advertised price of a scooty. If he makes a profit of ₹6,526 on the sale of the scooty, what is the advertised price (in ₹)?436", "options": [{"text": "25,132", "added": false}, {"text": "25,100", "added": false}, {"text": "25,103", "added": false}, {"text": "25,065", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "25,100"}, {"n": 18, "text": "Sohan sells a water bottle to Ronak at 28% profit. Ronak sells the water bottle to Rahul at a profit of 12.5%. If Rahul paid ₹288 for the water bottle, then for how much did Sohan buy it?", "options": [{"text": "₹200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹150", "added": false}, {"text": "₹180", "added": false}, {"text": "₹220", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "₹200"}, {"n": 19, "text": "The cost of a washing machine is 75% less than the cost of a TV. If the cost of the washing machine increases by 72% and that of the TV decreases by 20%, then what is the percentage change in the total cost of 4 washing machines and 3 TVs?", "options": [{"text": "Decrease by 8%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase by 6%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase by 3%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decrease by 1%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "Increase by 3%"}]}